MOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:

1. PRELIMINARY OBJECTIONS

   1.1 The present counter-petition is being filed by the Respondent in response to the petition filed by the Petitioner dated {{ original_petition_date }}.

   1.2 The Respondent submits that the petition filed by the Petitioner is misconceived, frivolous, and liable to be dismissed with exemplary costs.

2. FACTS OF THE CASE (AS PER ORIGINAL PETITION)

   {{ facts_of_case }}

3. RESPONDENT'S VERSION OF FACTS

   The Respondent submits the following true and correct facts:

   {{ counter_facts }}

4. LEGAL OBJECTIONS AND SUBMISSIONS

   4.1 The Respondent raises the following legal objections to the petition:

   {{ legal_objections }}

   4.2 The petition is not maintainable in law for the following reasons:
       - [Lack of cause of action]
       - [Violation of limitation period]
       - [Lack of jurisdiction]
       - [Non-joinder of necessary parties]
       - [Other legal grounds]

   4.3 The Petitioner has failed to disclose material facts and has made false and misleading statements in the petition.

   4.4 The petition is an abuse of the process of law and has been filed with malicious intent to harass the Respondent.

5. EVIDENCE AND DOCUMENTS

   The Respondent relies on the following evidence and documents in support of this counter-petition:

   {{ evidence_list }}

   Copies of all relevant documents are annexed herewith and marked as Annexures R-1 to R-[X].

6. LEGAL PROVISIONS

   The Respondent submits that the following legal provisions are applicable to the present case:

   6.1 [Relevant sections of applicable laws]
   6.2 [Relevant case law precedents]
   6.3 [Constitutional provisions, if applicable]

7. GROUNDS FOR DISMISSAL

   The Respondent submits that the petition is liable to be dismissed on the following grounds:

   7.1 The petition does not disclose any cause of action against the Respondent.
   
   7.2 The allegations made in the petition are false, frivolous, and vexatious.
   
   7.3 The Petitioner has not come to the Court with clean hands.
   
   7.4 The petition is barred by limitation.
   
   7.5 The petition is an abuse of the process of law.

8. COUNTER-CLAIM (IF ANY)

   Without prejudice to the above submissions, the Respondent hereby files the following counter-claim against the Petitioner:

   [Details of counter-claim, if any]

9. PRAYER

   In light of the above facts, legal submissions, and evidence, the Respondent most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:

   a) Dismiss the petition filed by the Petitioner with exemplary costs;

   b) {{ prayer_relief }}

   c) Award costs of this counter-petition to the Respondent;

   d) Pass any other order(s) that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

AND FOR THIS ACT OF KINDNESS, THE RESPONDENT SHALL DUTY BOUND FOREVER PRAY.

