IMPORTANT NOTES:

1. This counter-petition must be filed within the time limit prescribed by law (usually 30 days from service of notice/petition).

2. All facts stated must be true and verifiable. False statements may attract penalties under law.

3. All documentary evidence must be properly annexed and marked.

4. It is advisable to consult a qualified advocate before filing this counter-petition.

5. Keep copies of all documents and the court receipt for your records.

6. Attend all court hearings as per the schedule provided by the court.

